// Google Drive on the iPhone (docs/15 §2.4, §5.5; S4b-BL-117): the two build settings the app reads, set in this file
// for every configuration (project.yml: configFiles). **No real value is committed.** With an empty
// GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID the app's Settings > Google Drive says Drive is not available, as Android does without a client.
//
// To try Drive on your own build, put the owner's values in Config/Drive.local.xcconfig (git-ignored), not here:
//
//   GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID = <number>-<random>.apps.googleusercontent.com
//   GOOGLE_IOS_URL_SCHEME = com.googleusercontent.apps.<number>-<random>
//
// The first is Info.plist's GoogleIOSClientId (the iOS OAuth client of the Google Cloud project, bundle id app.doorprints,
// docs/15 §2.4); the second is that client id reversed, the redirect scheme Google gives with it ("iOS URL scheme"),
// registered in Info.plist's CFBundleURLTypes. The sign-in is ASWebAuthenticationSession with PKCE: no client secret, no
// Google SDK.
GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID =

// A scheme nothing redirects to, so the Info.plist entry is well-formed while no client is set.
GOOGLE_IOS_URL_SCHEME = app.doorprints.drive-not-configured

// The owner's own values, when there is such a file (an optional include: no error when it is absent).
#include? "Drive.local.xcconfig"
